# Mohawk street scene — character references

When generating or extending **gritty nightlife street** art for Mohawk (crowd shots, hero plates, reels):

## Mohawk figure

- Man with **black mohawk**, tight black clothes, **black jacket** (leather or similar) with **small patches**.
- Often **softened by vapor, steam, or haze** in crowd shots; may read sharper when he is a focal foreground figure.

## Reference female model 1

- **Center of frame**, walking **away from camera** (with model 2).
- Long **blonde wavy hair**.
- **Tight short black dress** (thin straps), **black high heels**.

## Reference female model 2

- Beside model 1, walking **away from camera**.
- Long **dark curly hair**.
- **Brown or tan jacket/vest** over **short black skirt**, **patterned lace leggings or stockings**, **dark boots**.

## Canonical Mohawk static hero

- **File:** `Site/img/mohawk-hero.jpg`
- **Source plate:** gritty neon crowd night (`mohawk-hero-gritty-street-source.jpg` in `NewTowerArtWork/img/`)
- Models 1 & 2 appear in the **center mid-ground** of this hero; Mohawk figure **foreground right**.

## Setting notes

- Night, dense crowd, traffic, neon, steam — see gritty-street studies in `NewTowerArtWork/img/gritty-street/` when needed.
- Distant **stone obelisk tower** optional in other plates; hero is **street-only** (no tower required in frame).
